in September 1965 as a joint venture between Hamlyn and [l=EMI] Records, selling low-cost reissues and also some original material. EMI provided the music and Hamlyn the publishing. The logo around this time has 'Paul Hamlyn' and 'EMI Records' circling the 'mfp' logo. \r\n\r\nMFP had offices in various cities including Amsterdam, Brussels, Johannesburg, Köln, London, Sydney, Paris and Stockholm.\r\n\r\nIn 1970, Hamlyn's parent company, International Publishing Group (IPC) was acquired by Reed Paper Group. One year later, EMI bought out Reed and took full control over Music For Pleasure. MFP remained an independent company in Belgium.  In September 1973, a parallel label called [l41886], was launched.\r\n\r\nMFP carried on throughout the '70s, but at the start of the '80s ran into trouble. This was due to changes in technology and major label rationalisations. MFP ended up as little more than a worldwide distribution network.\r\n\r\nThe new MUSIC FOR PLEASURE/EMI logo (9th image) was introduced approx. 1985. First on sleeves, later the traditional yellow vinyl labels were replaced by purple labels. Releases with this new logo and/or purple labels can't have a date prior to 1985.\r\n\r\nFrom the 3rd April 2006 MFP was revived under the control of [l=EMI Gold].\r\n\r\nPlease note, the '60s and '70s series of records for children with the [l161011] logo should be entered under that label name. These records have catalogue numbers beginning with 'No', 'Number' or FP. Please note that MFP later used the FP prefix for other releases. All singles released in the '80s with an FP cat# prefix are Music For Pleasure and not Surprise Surprise.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:18512","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":131854,"name":"Music For Pleasure Limited"},"sublabels":[{"id":694501,"name":"Back To The 60's"},{"id":3963930,"name":"Big Band Series (5)"},{"id":259366,"name":"Double Top"},{"id":2689859,"name":"Enregistrements Originaux / Coffret 3 Disques"},{"id":4421302,"name":"Guitar Boogie (2)"},{"id":1242526,"name":"Hits Of (2)"},{"id":680921,"name":"Hot Hits (3)"},{"id":305906,"name":"Hour Of Pleasure"},{"id":1839063,"name":"Junior Choice (2)"},{"id":853475,"name":"Les Plus Grands Artistes Du Monde Arabe"},{"id":2348887,"name":"Les Plus Grands Noms Du Rock"},{"id":81721,"name":"Listen For Pleasure"},{"id":4280962,"name":"Listen To The Band"},{"id":828312,"name":"Merry Go Round (2)"},{"id":1078252,"name":"MFP Exclusiv"},{"id":1688864,"name":"Mfp Series"},{"id":625624,"name":"MFP Super"},{"id":739338,"name":"Music For Pleasure Cassettes"},{"id":1821163,"name":"Music For Pleasure Classics"},{"id":835278,"name":"Music For Pleasure Premier"},{"id":109369,"name":"Music Melody"},{"id":1774668,"name":"Night Club (4)"},{"id":97675,"name":"Number One Records"},{"id":2410360,"name":"Original Recordings (6)"},{"id":292101,"name":"Plaisir Du Classique (2)"},{"id":2239102,"name":"Popular Classics Series (3)"},{"id":565191,"name":"Premier Jazz"},{"id":1157083,"name":"Pumpkin Records (8)"},{"id":305508,"name":"Savile's Time Travels"},{"id":798916,"name":"Songwriters Of The Century Series"},{"id":517542,"name":"Special Award Series"},{"id":1389676,"name":"Springbok Hit Parade"},{"id":407490,"name":"The Golden Age"},{"id":1122125,"name":"The Great Entertainers"},{"id":130357,"name":"The Jazz Club"},{"id":939405,"name":"Those Fabulous 50's"},{"id":531372,"name":"Two Of A Kind Series"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/18512-Music-For-Pleasure","type":"label","urls":["https://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/company/00851847","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_for_Pleasure_%28record_label%29"]}},"/api/discogs/label/1852259/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1852259","image":"https://i.discogs.com/NMHRFsOIcIK8cpNy-KP_DhfP_Yp0FamLYPs8P4q0XNs/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTE4NTIy/NTktMTU5Mjc2MzMy/NC05NTM1LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/vyPJ3sffNMS2xaQ6afg1U_XtCZD5wTvJwyTLYOR3v10/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTE4NTIy/NTktMTU5Mjc2MzMy/NC05NTM1LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Window on the World is half MP3 blog, half record label. It is an imprint of Dots Per Inch Music intended for the music of the internet that doesn’t ask for a label, but does need more than mere “posting-up.” \r\n\r\nWindow on the World offers basic distribution and the benefit of association when it comes to catalog opportunities such as creative synchronization, comprehensive delivery of music across territories, and basic publishing admin, all on a scalable opt-in/opt-out basis. WOW makes sure the pennies are picked up and that if a project takes off, things are well-oiled for a smooth start. ","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:1852259","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":1467987,"name":"Dots Per Inch Music"},"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/1852259-Window-on-the-World","type":"label","urls":["https://www.wotw.online","https://www.dpimusic.com/window-on-the-world"]}},"/api/discogs/label/3196691/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"3196691","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:3196691","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/3196691-Club-Yeke","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/4676124/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4676124","image":"https://i.discogs.com/uc_Ygh-F3cm9nut6Ee4PACRCDBo4rTlq0EP7cJ-CpQ4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTQ2NzYx/MjQtMTc4NzE1NDY2/NS03MzYwLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/gbN4IneuREBLNZPYH_6y4_7RH-_9wHfYohPRXPygo1c/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTQ2NzYx/MjQtMTc4NzE1NDY2/NS03MzYwLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"concept record label. anonymous releases, artist info found in the record sleeve.","